From 9aa0944d2d60c142274474d72ab842d9a89da829 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krispgece <329631437+krispgece@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:33:21 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] ImsService: Match the JNI of the Android 16 video
 telephony libraries

The video telephony libraries now come from an Android 16 build. Its
libmtk_vt_wrapper exports 16 natives instead of 21: nInitialization
takes a third, boolean argument, and nSetCameraParametersWithSim,
nSwitchFeature, nSnapshot, nStartRecording and nStopRecording are gone.
The JNI functions are looked up by name, so a stale declaration does
not fail to load; it passes a missing argument or throws
UnsatisfiedLinkError in the IMS process once it is called.

- nInitialization(II)I becomes (IIZ)I. Like Xiaomi's own Android 16
  ImsService, pass true when the call id comes from the 130 URC (a
  mobile-originated call) and false when the session is created with
  a call id (a mobile-terminated call). bind() hands the flag to the
  provider handler in Message.arg1.
- postEventFromNative calls nSetCameraParameters instead of
  nSetCameraParametersWithSim, as Xiaomi's does.
- switchFeatureInternal no longer calls nSwitchFeature. Xiaomi's drops
  the call as well and keeps only resetState(); the result was never
  used.
- Drop the declarations of the natives the library no longer has.
  Nothing calls nSnapshot, nStartRecording or nStopRecording.
